  Deep Explanation: The Two Solutions & Performance Impact                                                                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  ---
  Part 1 — Why Adding PP at All?                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Before explaining the solutions, it's worth understanding why PP is necessary and what performance it unlocks.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The Memory Wall Problem
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  ColossalAI's current autoparallelize() only searches over TP × DP. The ILP solver (solver.py) assigns one of: replicate weight, shard along axis 0, shard along axis 1, etc. — all within a single flat device mesh.                                         
   
  The fundamental limit: TP is bounded by intra-node bandwidth. NVLink gives ~600 GB/s within a node (8 GPUs), but across nodes you only get ~100-200 GB/s InfiniBand. If your TP all-reduce has to cross nodes, throughput collapses. So in practice T ≤ 8    
  (within one node).
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  With T=8 and D=data-parallel replicas:                                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  - GPT-2 (1.5B): fits comfortably, TP+DP is fine
  - GPT-6.7B: still fits with T=8, needs careful memory management                                                                                                                                                                                             
  - GPT-13B: marginal, may OOM even with T=8 + ZeRO               
  - GPT-30B+: cannot fit without PP, period                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  PP solves this by splitting the model vertically — stage 0 holds layers 0–11, stage 1 holds layers 12–23, etc. — so each GPU only holds 1/P of the model parameters.                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The Communication Topology Argument                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  This is the most important performance reason to add PP:                                                                                                                                                                                                     
                  
  Without PP (TP+DP only):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
    Every transformer layer: AllReduce across T GPUs
    For 12 layers × 2 AllReduces each (fwd+bwd) = 24 collectives per step
    If T spans multiple nodes → all 24 collectives cross slow interconnect                                                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  With PP (TP within node, PP across nodes):                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
    TP AllReduces happen within one node (fast NVLink, ~600 GB/s)                                                                                                                                                                                              
    PP sends activation tensor once at each stage boundary (typically small)                                                                                                                                                                                   
    Effectively: expensive TP comms stay on fast rail, PP uses slow rail cheaply                                                                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Megatron-LM paper (NVIDIA, 2021) showed that for large models on multi-node clusters, PP+TP+DP achieves 52% GPU utilization while TP-only across nodes gets ~30% because the cross-node TP all-reduce kills throughput.                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  Part 2 — Solution B (Heuristic, Phase 1): Uniform TP + Auto Pipeline
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  What it does
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  You constrain the search so every pipeline stage must use the same TP degree. Then:                                                                                                                                                                          
  1. alpa_dp auto-finds: how many stages, and which layers go to which stage                                                                                                                                                                                   
  2. initialize_model auto-finds: the best TP/DP plan within each stage (same T for all stages)                                                                                                                                                                
  3. No resharding at stage boundaries needed (all stages output the same sharding spec)       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Concrete example — GPT-6.7B on 8 GPUs                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Without this plan, autoparallelize() might choose TP=8, DP=1 (all 8 GPUs tensor-parallel). With uniform-TP auto-pipeline:                                                                                                                                    
                  
  alpa_dp might find:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
    Stage 0 (embedding, layers 0-3):  TP=2, DP=2  →  4 GPUs                                                                                                                                                                                                    
    Stage 1 (layers 4-15):            TP=2, DP=2  →  4 GPUs                                                                                                                                                                                                    
    Total: 8 GPUs, 2 pipeline stages                                                                                                                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Or alternatively:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
    Stage 0 (layers 0-7):   TP=4, DP=1  →  4 GPUs
    Stage 1 (layers 8-15):  TP=4, DP=1  →  4 GPUs                                                                                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The DP solver picks whichever assignment minimizes (B-1) × max_stage_cost + sum_stage_costs, where cost comes from initialize_model()'s ILP objective. This is strictly better than naive equal-size splitting which most frameworks do by default.          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Performance gain over current TP+DP only                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
                  
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┐                                                                                                                                                          
  │                  Scenario                  │       TP+DP only        │  TP+DP+PP (uniform TP)   │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                                                          
  │ Model fits in single node                  │ Small gain (~5-15%)     │ Better memory efficiency │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
  │ Model requires cross-node TP               │ Poor (slow all-reduces) │ Large gain (1.5-2×)      │                                                                                                                                                          
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                                                          
  │ Model doesn't fit with T=8                 │ Cannot train            │ Enables training         │                                                                                                                                                          
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                                                          
  │ Uneven layer compute (embedding vs blocks) │ One plan for all        │ Per-stage plan           │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘                                                                                                                                                          
                  
  The gain from keeping TP intra-node while using PP cross-node is where the biggest speedup comes from.                                                                                                                                                       
                  
  The bubble overhead — when does PP hurt?                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
                  
  PP introduces a pipeline bubble: time wasted waiting for previous microbatches. For 1F1B scheduling:                                                                                                                                                         
   
  bubble_fraction = (P - 1) / (B + P - 1)                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
                  
  Where P = pipeline stages, B = microbatches.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
   
  - P=4, B=4: bubble = 3/7 ≈ 43% wasted — PP is bad here                                                                                                                                                                                                       
  - P=4, B=16: bubble = 3/19 ≈ 16% wasted — acceptable
  - P=4, B=64: bubble = 3/67 ≈ 4% wasted — negligible                                                                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  So alpa_dp's formula cost = sum_stage_costs + (B-1) × max_stage_cost automatically discourages too many pipeline stages when B is small, and allows more stages when B is large. This is why auto-search beats manual configuration — a human would need to  
  compute this tradeoff manually for each model/cluster combo.                                                                                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
