  Part 3 — Solution A (Optimal, Phase 2): Heterogeneous TP via Slice-Gather
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  What it adds over Solution B
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  In Solution B, embedding layers and transformer blocks all use the same TP degree. But these layers have fundamentally different compute profiles:                                                                                                           
   
  - Embedding layer: mostly memory-bandwidth bound, small compute, benefits from DP not TP                                                                                                                                                                     
  - Transformer blocks: heavily compute-bound, benefits from TP
  - LM head: large vocab projection, should shard differently                                                                                                                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  With heterogeneous TP per stage (Solution A), alpa_dp can assign:                                                                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Stage 0 (embedding):          TP=1, DP=4  →  better bandwidth utilization                                                                                                                                                                                    
  Stage 1-3 (transformer):      TP=4, DP=1  →  compute-optimal                                                                                                                                                                                                 
  Stage 4 (LM head):            TP=2, DP=2  →  balanced                                                                                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Galvatron's paper shows this gives ~10-20% additional throughput over uniform TP on models with heterogeneous layer types (MoE models gain even more, 30%+).                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The Slice-Gather mechanism — what actually happens at the boundary                                                                                                                                                                                           
                  
  When Stage 0 (TP=1) finishes and sends activations to Stage 1 (TP=4):                                                                                                                                                                                        
                  
  Stage 0 output: full tensor [batch, seq, hidden]                                                                                                                                                                                                             
                      on 1 GPU (no sharding)                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
                            ↓                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  
                BoundarySplit (scatter along hidden dim)                                                                                                                                                                                                       
                            ↓                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  
  Stage 1 input: [batch, seq, hidden/4]
                 on 4 GPUs (column-sharded for TP)                                                                                                                                                                                                             
                  
  When Stage 1 (TP=4) sends to Stage 2 (TP=1):                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
  Stage 1 output: [batch, seq, hidden/4]
                  on 4 GPUs (row-sharded)                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
                            ↓                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  
                BoundaryAllGather (gather along hidden dim)
                            ↓                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  
  Stage 2 input: [batch, seq, hidden]                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
                 on 1 GPU (full tensor)
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  These ops have autograd support so gradients flow correctly in the backward pass (the forward gather becomes a backward split, and vice versa). The cost is one extra collective per stage boundary — much cheaper than TP all-reduces on every layer.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Why the cost model matters here                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  For the DP to find the right plan, the cost of the boundary all-gather/split must be included in compute_cost[k, i, m, 0]. The activation tensor at the boundary has size batch × seq_len × hidden, so:                                                      
                  
  boundary_comm_cost = alpha + beta × (batch × seq_len × hidden × 2 bytes)                                                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  If this isn't included, the DP might assign radically different TP degrees to adjacent stages thinking it's "free," but the runtime then incurs unexpected communication overhead.                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
