   Question 1: Does Current ColossalAI Support Cross-Node Training?                                                                                                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Yes, fully. ColossalAI supports cross-node training through multiple launchers, all using NCCL over TCP:                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  # torchrun (most common):
  colossalai.launch_from_torch()                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  # reads MASTER_ADDR, MASTER_PORT, RANK, LOCAL_RANK, WORLD_SIZE from env
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  # SLURM cluster:
  colossalai.launch_from_slurm(host=..., port=...)                                                                                                                                                                                                             
  # reads SLURM_PROCID, SLURM_NPROCS                                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  
  # OpenMPI:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
  colossalai.launch_from_openmpi(host=..., port=...)
  # reads OMPI_COMM_WORLD_RANK, etc.                                                                                                                                                                                                                           
                  
  Under the hood, initialize.py:59 calls torch.distributed.init_process_group(backend="nccl", init_method="tcp://..."). NCCL handles both intra-node (NVLink/PCIe) and cross-node (InfiniBand/RoCE/Ethernet) automatically — the process group is purely based 
  on global ranks, not physical locations.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  All the relevant components are cross-node aware:                                                                                                                                                                                                            
  
  ┌──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐                                                                                                                  
  │        Component         │                                          How it handles cross-node                                           │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ ProcessGroupMesh         │ Pure math on global ranks — unravel(rank, shape) works regardless of which node a rank is on                 │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ DeviceMesh               │ physical_mesh_id is a tensor of global ranks — can span nodes                                                │                                                                                                                  
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                  
  │ AlphaBetaProfiler        │ Profiles pairwise (GPU_i, GPU_j) latency — captures cross-node vs intra-node bandwidth difference explicitly │                                                                                                                  
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                  
  │ PipelineP2PCommunication │ Uses NCCL isend/irecv — native cross-node P2P over InfiniBand                                                │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                                                                                                                  
  │ PipelineStageManager     │ Built on ProcessGroupMesh — topology-agnostic                                                                │
  └──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                                                                                                                  
                  
