  Question 2: Will Auto Pipeline Still Work Cross-Node After Adding It?
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Yes, and it will work significantly better cross-node than without PP.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The components already have multi-host support built in                                                                                                                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Looking at calc_pipeline_strategy.py:6, get_submesh_choices explicitly takes num_hosts:                                                                                                                                                                      
                  
  def get_submesh_choices(num_hosts, num_devices_per_host, mode="new"):                                                                                                                                                                                        
      # In "alpa" mode: generates multi-host submeshes like (2, 8), (3, 8)
      for i in range(2, num_hosts + 1):                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
          submesh_choices.append((i, num_devices_per_host))
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  So with 2 nodes × 8 GPUs = 16 devices, the submesh choices include:                                                                                                                                                                                          
  - (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 4), (1, 8) — single-node submeshes (intra-node TP)                                                                                                                                                                                     
  - (2, 8) — both nodes full (cross-node, used for large stages)                                                                                                                                                                                               
                                                                
  The DeviceMesh sub-carving in the orchestrator assigns global ranks, and PipelineStageManager uses ProcessGroupMesh which maps to the same global rank space. No code in the pipeline path assumes ranks are on the same physical node.                      
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  The cost model automatically learns to prefer the cross-node topology                                                                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  This is the key insight. AlphaBetaProfiler (alpha_beta_profiler.py:26) profiles every pair (GPU_i, GPU_j) independently and stores different (alpha, beta) values for intra-node vs cross-node pairs:                                                        
  
  # From the profiler docstring (real measured values):                                                                                                                                                                                                        
  # Intra-node pair (GPU 0, GPU 1): alpha=1.96e-05,  beta=4.74e-12  ← fast NVLink                                                                                                                                                                              
  # Cross-node pair (GPU 0, GPU 4): alpha=1.95e-05,  beta=6.97e-11  ← slower InfiniBand                                                                                                                                                                        
  #                                                         ↑ 14× higher beta cross-node                                                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  When initialize_model() computes the ILP objective for a stage assigned to a cross-node submesh (e.g., TP=16 spanning two nodes), the communication cost uses the high cross-node beta. The same stage assigned to an intra-node submesh (TP=8 on one node)  
  gets the low beta. The DP solver then naturally prefers:                                                                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Stage 0: submesh (1, 8) → TP=8, all on Node 0  (fast NVLink all-reduces)
  Stage 1: submesh (1, 8) → TP=8, all on Node 1  (fast NVLink all-reduces)                                                                                                                                                                                     
  PP communication (activation send/recv): cross-node once per stage boundary (cheap)                                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  over:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
  No PP: submesh (2, 8) → TP=16, spanning both nodes (slow cross-node all-reduces every layer)                                                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                              
  The auto-planner discovers the "TP intra-node, PP cross-node" topology automatically because the alpha-beta cost model makes cross-node TP expensive. You don't need to hardcode this knowledge — the solver finds it.                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
